---
// Plain-language terms of use.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../content/site';

const app = siteConfig.appName;
const email = siteConfig.contactEmail;
---
<LegalLayout title="Terms of use">
  <p class="lead">
    These terms are the ground rules for using {app}. They're short and written in plain language. By using {app}, you
    agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>What {app} is</h2>
  <p>
    {app} is a small, free, invite-only app for two people to coach each other: set each other's workout and diet
    plans, log progress and share it. It's run by individuals, not a company, and it isn't a medical or professional
    fitness service.
  </p>

  <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    Plans in {app} are written by your partner or by you, not by a doctor, dietitian or certified trainer. Nothing in
    the app is medical advice. Check with a qualified professional before starting a new exercise or diet programme,
    especially if you have a health condition, are pregnant, or are changing your weight quickly. The app warns about
    very low calorie targets, but it's your call (and your partner's) to keep plans safe. Stop and get help if
    something hurts or feels wrong.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need an invite (or to be one of the people who run {app}) and a Google account to join.</li>
    <li>Keep your Google account secure; anyone who can sign in to it can sign in to {app} as you.</li>
    <li>One account per person, and you can be paired with one partner at a time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your content</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      What you add (logs, photos, messages, plans you write) stays yours. You let {app} store it and show it to you and
      your paired partner, which is what the app needs to work. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Only upload photos you have the right to share, and don't upload photos of other people without their permission.
    </li>
    <li>Be kind. Don't use {app} to harass, threaten or harm anyone, including your partner.</li>
    <li>Don't try to break, overload or get around the app's security or limits, or access anyone else's data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ending things</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can unpair or delete your account at any time from Settings.</li>
    <li>
      The people who run {app} may deactivate an account that breaks these terms or puts others at risk. A deactivated
      account can't sign in, and its data is kept unless the person asks us (by email) to delete it.
    </li>
    <li>
      {app} is provided free and as-is. We do our best to keep it running and your data safe, but we can't promise it
      will always be available or error-free, and we may change or shut down the app. If we plan to shut it down, we'll
      give notice in the app so you can save what you need.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Limits on responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, the people who run {app} aren't responsible for injuries, health outcomes or losses
    that come from following a plan, or from the app being unavailable or losing data. Nothing here limits rights you
    have under consumer law that can't be limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms, we'll update this page and its effective date. If you keep using {app} after a change,
    the new terms apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
